AWS Auto Scaling for EC2 Instances
Scenario:
You run a web application on EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Traffic varies throughout the day, so you want to automatically scale the number of EC2 instances to maintain performance and reduce costs.

Step 1: Create a Launch Template
Define the instance configuration (AMI, instance type, security groups, user data):

bash
aws ec2 create-launch-template --launch-template-name WebAppLaunchTemplate \
  --version-description "v1" \
  --launch-template-data '{
        "ImageId":"ami-0abcdef1234567890",
        "InstanceType":"t3.medium",
        "SecurityGroupIds":["sg-0123456789abcdef0"],
        "UserData":"IyEvYmluL2Jhc2gKZWNobyAiSGVsbG8sIFdvcmxkISIgPiAvdmFyL3d3dy9odG1sL2luZGV4Lmh0bWw="
      }'
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 2: Create an Auto Scaling Group (ASG)
bash
aws autoscaling create-auto-scaling-group \
  --auto-scaling-group-name MyWebAppASG \
  --launch-template "LaunchTemplateName=WebAppLaunchTemplate,Version=1" \
  --min-size 2 \
  --max-size 6 \
  --desired-capacity 2 \
  --vpc-zone-identifier "subnet-abcde123,subnet-bcdef234" \
  --target-group-arns "arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:region:account-id:targetgroup/my-target-group/0123456789abcdef"
ASG launches instances into specified subnets.

Attaches instances to the ALB target group.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 3: Set up Scaling Policies
Configure a target tracking scaling policy to keep average CPU utilization at ~50%.

bash
aws autoscaling put-scaling-policy \
  --auto-scaling-group-name MyWebAppASG \
  --policy-name CPU50PercentScalingPolicy \
  --policy-type TargetTrackingScaling \
  --target-tracking-configuration '{
      "PredefinedMetricSpecification": {"PredefinedMetricType": "ASGAverageCPUUtilization"},
      "TargetValue": 50.0,
      "DisableScaleIn": false
    }'
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 4: (Optional) Configure Notifications
Set up notifications when scaling events occur:

bash
aws autoscaling put-notification-configuration \
  --auto-scaling-group-name MyWebAppASG \
  --topic-arn arn:aws:sns:region:account-id:MyScalingTopic \
  --notification-types "autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH" "autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATE"

