AWS Auto Scaling for ECS Tasks
Scenario:
You have a containerized microservice deployed using Amazon ECS with Fargate launch type. You want to automatically adjust the number of running tasks based on CPU usage or custom CloudWatch metrics.

Step 1: Define ECS Service with Desired Count
Create ECS service running 2 tasks:

bash
aws ecs create-service \
  --cluster my-ecs-cluster \
  --service-name my-api-service \
  --task-definition my-api-task-def:1 \
  --desired-count 2 \
  --launch-type FARGATE \
  --network-configuration 'awsvpcConfiguration={subnets=[subnet-abcde123],securityGroups=[sg-01234abcde],assignPublicIp="ENABLED"}' \
  --load-balancers '[{"targetGroupArn":"arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:region:account-id:targetgroup/my-tg/abcdef123456","containerName":"my-api-container","containerPort":80}]'
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 2: Enable ECS Service Auto Scaling
Attach an IAM role for ECS Auto Scaling:

bash
aws iam create-service-linked-role --aws-service-name ecs.application-autoscaling.amazonaws.com
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 3: Create Application Auto Scaling Target
Register scalable target for the ECS service:

bash
aws application-autoscaling register-scalable-target \
  --service-namespace ecs \
  --resource-id service/my-ecs-cluster/my-api-service \
  --scalable-dimension ecs:service:DesiredCount \
  --min-capacity 2 --max-capacity 10
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 4: Create Target Tracking Scaling Policy
Scale tasks to maintain average CPU utilization at 50%:

bash
aws application-autoscaling put-scaling-policy \
  --policy-name cpu-target-tracking-policy \
  --service-namespace ecs \
  --resource-id service/my-ecs-cluster/my-api-service \
  --scalable-dimension ecs:service:DesiredCount \
  --policy-type TargetTrackingScaling \
  --target-tracking-scaling-policy-configuration '{
      "TargetValue": 50,
      "PredefinedMetricSpecification": {
          "PredefinedMetricType": "ECSServiceAverageCPUUtilization"
      },
      "ScaleInCooldown": 60,
      "ScaleOutCooldown": 60
  }'
----------------------------------------------------------
Real-World Use Case Summary
Web Application on EC2 Instances: Automatically adjust number of web servers based on traffic spike (CPU usage or request count), maintaining performance and minimizing cost.

Microservices on ECS Fargate: Dynamically scale backend microservices container tasks in response to load, improving resource efficiency and customer experience.

Integration: Both EC2 and ECS can leverage AWS Application Auto Scaling with CloudWatch alarms and custom metrics for fine-tuned scaling control.

This dynamic scaling capability of AWS Auto Scaling optimizes cost, ensures high availability, and matches compute resources to real-time demand without manual intervention.
